  displayName: Amanita
  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 30b6047a6db38e14e8b81a696888117a, type: 3}
  description: 'Amanita muscaria, commonly known as the fly agaric or fly amanita.

    Poisonous.
    Hallucinogenic.

    Have a brilliant red cap generally covered with warts that
    are the remnant of the universal veil that covers the young mushrooms as they
    grow. The warts are typically visible, but can be removed by rain.'
